# =============================================================================
# Deny-by-default .gitignore for a public GitHub Pages repository.
#
# Strategy: deny everything, then re-allow an explicit allowlist of individual
# files. A new file is invisible to git until someone adds a rule for it on
# purpose. This inverts the usual failure mode, where a forgotten pattern
# silently leaks a file.
#
# IMPORTANT — how this actually works:
#   `/*` only denies TOP-LEVEL entries. The moment a directory is re-allowed,
#   git descends into it and its contents are no longer covered. So every
#   allowed directory must be re-denied with `dir/*` before naming the files
#   inside it. Miss that step and the whole allowlist quietly fails open.
#
#   Files are named INDIVIDUALLY rather than by extension. An extension glob
#   such as `!/assets/img/*.png` re-allows every PNG dropped into that
#   directory — including one whose filename names a client.
#
# To publish a new asset: add an explicit `!` rule for it. Nothing else works.
# Verify with:  git add -A && git diff --cached --name-only
# =============================================================================

# ---- 1. Deny everything at the root -----------------------------------------
/*

# ---- 2. Re-allow root-level published files ---------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/.nojekyll
!/index.html
!/404.html
!/evolution.html
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml
!/README.md
!/LICENSE

# ---- 3. assets/ -------------------------------------------------------------
!/assets/
/assets/*
!/assets/img/
/assets/img/*
!/assets/img/portrait.jpg
!/assets/img/portrait-cutout.webp
!/assets/img/np-mark.webp
!/assets/img/contact-scene.webp
!/assets/img/favicon.svg

# ---- 3b. stories/ -----------------------------------------------------------
!/stories/
/stories/*
!/stories/offline-field-systems.html
!/stories/spatial-measurement.html
!/stories/enterprise-modernisation.html
!/stories/agentic-workflows.html
!/stories/connected-devices.html

# ---- 4. css/ ----------------------------------------------------------------
!/css/
/css/*
!/css/site.css

# ---- 5. js/ -----------------------------------------------------------------
!/js/
/js/*
!/js/site.js

# ---- 6. Backstop denies -----------------------------------------------------
# The allowlist above should already exclude all of these. They are repeated as
# defence in depth, so that a future edit which loosens the allowlist does not
# immediately expose secrets, source maps or private tooling.

# Secrets and credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.mobileprovision
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*credential*
**/*secret*
**/*token*
**/.npmrc
**/.netrc

# Source maps and build metadata — never publish these
**/*.map
**/stats.json
**/build-manifest.json

# Tooling / editor / agent configuration
**/.claude/
**/.cursor/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.github/
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md

# OS and editor noise
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini
**/*.swp
**/*~

# Logs, dumps, archives, backups
**/*.log
**/*.bak
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/*.zip
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.bundle
**/*.sql
**/*.sqlite*

# Documents that tend to carry private content
**/*.pdf
**/*.docx
**/*.xlsx
**/*.pptx

# Raw / original media (unstripped metadata risk)
**/*.heic
**/*.tiff
**/*.raw
**/*.psd
**/*-original.*
**/*-raw.*

# Dependencies and build systems have no place in this repo
**/node_modules/
**/package.json
**/package-lock.json
**/yarn.lock
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/dist/
**/build/
